        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Cape Town</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1652 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-van-riebeeck">Jan van Riebeeck</a> and other employees of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> landed on 6 April 1652 to establish a permanent station at the Cape; Khoe and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-people">San peoples</a> had lived in the region long before.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/table-bay">Table Bay</a>, at the foot of Table Mountain, on the Cape Peninsula in the Western Cape of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Khoe and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-people">San peoples</a> of the Cape; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>'s station of 1652; the Castle of Good Hope; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> and its end; the Cape Qualified Franchise; District Six and the forced removals of apartheid; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robben-island">Robben Island</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>'s first public speech after his release</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Cape Town is the legislative capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, the seat of its Parliament, and the capital of the Western Cape.</span></div>
